==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱerh₂-}}

{{inh+|en|enm|cerebrum}}, from {{der|en|la|cerebrum||a brain; a skull}}; see there for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛ.ɹɪb.ɹəm/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cerebrum.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/səˈɹi.bɹəm/|/ˈsɛɹ.əb.ɹəm/|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛɹɪbɹəm|iːbɹəm|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cerebra|+}}

# {{lb|en|neuroanatomy}} The [[principal]] and most [[anterior]] part of the [[brain]] in [[vertebrate]]s, which is located in the [[front]] area of the [[skull]] and divided into two [[hemisphere]]s, [[left]] and [[right]], separated by a [[fissure]]. In [[human]]s it is the largest part of the brain and is [[responsible]] for the [[integration]] of [[complex]] [[sensory]] functions and the [[initiation]] and [[coordination]] of [[voluntary]] activity, and the higher [[mental]] functions such as [[consciousness]], [[thought]], [[reason]], [[emotion]], and [[memory]].
#: {{syn|en|telencephalon}}
#: {{hypo|en|cerebral hemisphere|cerebral cortex}}
#: {{holo|en|forebrain}}

